sound is equal to: (K = Constant)","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08cd","isCorrect":false,"choice":"K √ temperature (°F) knots"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ce","isCorrect":true,"choice":"K √ temperature (°K) knots"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08cf","isCorrect":false,"choice":"K √ temperature (°C. knots"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"K √ temperature (°K) metres per second"}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?resize=780%2C397&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33205 size-full size-big\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?resize=780%2C397&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"780\" height=\"397\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?w=838&amp;ssl=1 838w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?resize=300%2C153&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?resize=768%2C390&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-122600.png?resize=660%2C336&amp;ssl=1 660w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e76","question":"At FL 350 with a JSA deviation of -12, the true airspeed when flying at M 0.78 is","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"460 kt"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"436 kt"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"447 kt"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"490 kt"}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-123219.png?resize=510%2C740&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33206 size-full\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-123219.png?resize=510%2C740&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"510\" height=\"740\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-123219.png?w=510&amp;ssl=1 510w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-123219.png?resize=207%2C300&amp;ssl=1 207w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 510px) 100vw, 510px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e77","question":"Below is a schematic diagram of a Machmeter. Parts A, B, C and D are:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ratio arm, mach no pointer, static pressure inlet, ranging arm."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d6","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ranging arm, limiting mach no index, static pressure inlet, ratio arm."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"main shaft, TAS index, pitot pressure inlet, ranging arm."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d8","isCorrect":true,"choice":"ranging arm, limiting mach no index, pitot inlet, main shaft."}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/05AC81FE-1B75-495C-969F-71E9F12BB5DB.jpeg?fit=904%2C449&ssl=1","explanation":"<p>The Machmeter as a whole measures the ratio of the aircraft’s true airspeed to the local speed of sound. The <strong>pitot inlet (C)</strong> collects dynamic air pressure, while the internal static pressure system provides a reference. These pressures are compared using diaphragms and transmitted through the <strong>ranging arm (A)</strong> and <strong>main shaft (D)</strong> to move the needle. The <strong>limiting Mach index (B)</strong> serves as a safety marker for pilots to monitor.</p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e78","question":"When climbing at a constant mach number below the tropopause through an inversion:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08d9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the CAS and TAS will both increase."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08da","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the CAS and TAS will both decrease."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08db","isCorrect":true,"choice":"the CAS will decrease and the TAS will increase."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08dc","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the CAS will increase and the TAS will decrease."}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=780%2C935&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33208 size-full size-big\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=780%2C935&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"780\" height=\"935\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?w=1068&amp;ssl=1 1068w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=250%2C300&amp;ssl=1 250w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=854%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 854w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=768%2C920&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_14-12-19.jpg?resize=660%2C791&amp;ssl=1 660w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e79","question":"When descending below the tropopause under normal conditions (increasing temperature) at a constant CAS:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08dd","isCorrect":true,"choice":"both TAS and mach number will decrease."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08de","isCorrect":false,"choice":"both TAS and mach number will increase."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08df","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the TAS will decrease and the mach number will increase."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the TAS will increase and the mach number will decrease."}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_13-43-41.jpg?resize=477%2C1280&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33207 size-full\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_13-43-41.jpg?resize=477%2C1280&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"477\" height=\"1280\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_13-43-41.jpg?w=477&amp;ssl=1 477w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_13-43-41.jpg?resize=112%2C300&amp;ssl=1 112w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_13-43-41.jpg?resize=382%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 382w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 477px) 100vw, 477px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e7a","question":"Cruising at FL390, M 0.84 is found to give a TAS of 499 kt. The ISA deviation at this level will be:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"-17"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"+17"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"+19"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"-19"}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150013.png?resize=488%2C512&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33209 size-full\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150013.png?resize=488%2C512&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"488\" height=\"512\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150013.png?w=488&amp;ssl=1 488w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150013.png?resize=286%2C300&amp;ssl=1 286w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 488px) 100vw, 488px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e7b","question":"The errors to which the machmeter is subject are:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"instrument error, position error, compressibility error and manoeuvre induced error."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e6","isCorrect":true,"choice":"instrument error, position error and manoeuvre induced error."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"instrument error, position error, barometric error, temperature error and manoeuvre induced error."},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e8","isCorrect":false,"choice":"instrument error, position error, density error and manoeuvre induced error."}],"explanation":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Blockage Errors</strong></li>\n<li><strong>lag</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Instrument</strong></li>\n<li><strong> Position Errors</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Maneuver-Induced Errors</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e7c","question":"The relationships between TAS, mach number (MNo) and local speed of sound (LSS) is:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08e9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"LSS = MNo / TAS"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ea","isCorrect":false,"choice":"MNo = LSS / TAS"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08eb","isCorrect":true,"choice":"TAS = MNo x LSS"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ec","isCorrect":false,"choice":"MNo = LSS x TAS"}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?resize=780%2C321&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33210 size-full size-big\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?resize=780%2C321&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"780\" height=\"321\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?w=916&amp;ssl=1 916w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?resize=300%2C123&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?resize=768%2C316&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Screenshot-2024-12-04-150741.png?resize=660%2C272&amp;ssl=1 660w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e7d","question":"The machmeter gives an indication of mach number by measuring the ratio:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ed","isCorrect":false,"choice":"pitot pressure / static pressure"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ee","isCorrect":false,"choice":"static pressure / dynamic pressure"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08ef","isCorrect":false,"choice":"dynamic pressure / pitot pressure"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08f0","isCorrect":true,"choice":"dynamic pressure/ static pressure"}],"explanation":"<p>he Machmeter gives an indication of Mach number by measuring the ratio of <strong>dynamic to static pressure</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>dynamic:</strong> Represents the pressure from the aircraft’s forward motion through the air.</p>\n<p><strong>Static pressure:</strong> Represents the ambient pressure surrounding the aircraft.</p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"},{"difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7e7e","question":"An aircraft is flying at FL350 with a JSA deviation of +8. The mach no is 0.83 and the TAS 485. If the aircraft descends to FL300 and maintains the same mach no and TAS, the JSA deviation will now be:","choices":[{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08f1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"+8"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08f2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"-2"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08f3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"+2"},{"_id":"693e81fb6a1995dddc7b08f4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"-18"}],"image":"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_16-59-54.jpg?resize=292%2C1024&ssl=1","explanation":"<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-33215 size-large\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_16-59-54.jpg?resize=292%2C1024&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"292\" height=\"1024\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_16-59-54.jpg?resize=292%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 292w, https://i0.wp.com/eatpl.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/photo_2024-12-04_16-59-54.jpg?w=365&amp;ssl=1 365w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 292px) 100vw, 292px\"></p>\n","subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Machmeter"}]